# Docker reads .dockerignore from the BUILD CONTEXT ROOT, not from the directory
# holding the Dockerfile. Both compose services build with `context: ..`, so the
# context root is the repository root and this file must live here. A copy under
# docker/ is silently ignored — which is exactly how a 652 MB context and a
# Windows-built node_modules once reached the image (D-34).
#
# Patterns are matched against paths relative to the context root, and a bare
# name is NOT recursive: `node_modules` matches only ./node_modules and would
# leave frontend/node_modules in the context. Hence `**/`.

# Dependencies. These are installed inside the image from the lockfile; copying a
# host-built tree in would overwrite that install with the wrong platform's
# binaries and, under pnpm, with symlinks pointing at absolute host paths.
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc

# Build output. Regenerated in the image; a stale host copy is worse than none.
**/.next
**/out
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Secrets. Runtime configuration is injected by compose, never baked into a layer.
**/.env*

# Logs
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*
**/.pnpm-debug.log*

# Not needed to build, and large
.git
.gitignore
.github
docs
.vercel
.vscode
.idea
